 "summary": "The formal statements define R_k(3) as the least n such that every k-colouring of the edges of K_n has a monochromatic triangle. They then assert four things: (i) R_k(3)^{1/k} → ∞; (ii) for every k ≥ 2, R_k(3) ≥ (k^{1/3}/(6e^{38} log k))^k, together with (i); (iii) for every ε > 0 and all large k, (1/3−ε) k log k ≤ log R_k(3) ≤ (1+ε) k log k; (iv) log R_k(3) = Θ(k log k). The definitions match the standard notion, and the statements match or strengthen Theorem 1.1. The only notable caveat is that Lean fixes the explicit constant c = 1/(6e^{38}) where the paper only asserts some c > 0 (Lean is stronger); the Shannon-capacity reformulation is not formalized.",
